    "id": "moc100-22",
    "source_exam": "ABPMR MOC100 (September 2015 release)",
    "question_text": "A 55-year-old multiparous woman with a history of mild stress urinary incontinence has significant urinary incontinence after a stroke. A cystometrogram performed with electromyographic monitoring of the external urinary sphincter is normal. Potentially useful pharmacologic interventions include",
    "option_a": "cholinergic agonists",
