    "id": "pmr100-82",
    "source_exam": "ABPMR PM&R100 Part I (June 2015 release)",
    "question_text": "A 29-year-old dancer presents with pain that originates on the sole of her foot. She is tender to palpation along the anterior calcaneus and medial arch. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
    "option_a": "Calcaneal bursitis",
    "option_b": "Tibiotalar impingement",
