    "question_text": "A 22 year-old man was in his usual state of health until this morning. He noticed upon awakening that he had difficulty closing his right eyelid and moving his right mouth. He also noticed that his breakfast did not taste right. He went to school, but his teacher advised that he go to the emergency room when he saw him. On examination, he had weakness of orbicularis oris and orbicularis oculi with reduced taste sensation. You do not note any other cranial nerve, sensory, strength or reflex abnormalities. What is the next best step?",
