    "question_text": "A 31 year-old previously healthy woman presents with 3 days of painful loss of vision in one eye. Her fundoscopic examination is normal bilaterally. On light examination of her pupils, her left eye reacts normally to light. Upon swinging the penlight to the right eye, her pupil dilates. On repeat examination, these findings are reproducible. Otherwise, her cranial nerve, sensory, motor, reflexes 1 Neuroanatomy and cerebellar examination are normal. Which of the following is the most likely cause of her symptoms?",
