    "question_text": "A 35 year old woman with a history of headaches since she was 17 comes to you complaining of recurrent headaches for many years. Her headaches occur once a week in the frontal area, are very intense and throbbing in characteristic lasting 2 hours without taking any medicine. The headaches are associated with nausea but no vomiting, no photophobia or phonophobia. What characteristic makes this headache less likely a migraine?",
