    "question_text": "A 48 year old man presents to the emergency room with a severe headache. He has never had headaches before. On exam he is lethargic and has right sided weakness. You suspect that he may have suffered a subarachnoid hemorrhage. Which characteristic below would be more likely to increase his risk for an aneurysmal rupture causing his symptoms?",
