    "correct_option": "A",
    "explanation": "The correct answer is A. This patient has trigeminal neuralgia. Neurovascular compression is the cause of the majority of cases of trigeminal neuralgia. Most often a vascular loop is indenting the trigeminal nerve root and causes the classic unilateral neuralgic pain of trigeminal neuralgia. Multiple sclerosis patients are at a 20 times higher risk of trigeminal neuralgia compared to the general population but this is not the most common cause of trigeminal neuralgia. Posterior fossa mass, aneurysm, or Chiari malformation should all be considered and 15% of cases of trigeminal neuralgia are found to have a structural cause but again are not the most common cause (Cheshire 2015).",
