    "question_text": "A 55 year old woman presents to your office with new onset headaches. Her headaches started after she fell in the bathroom 2 weeks ago. She did lose ­consciousness after this fall but awoke less than a minute later with no neurological complaints except for headaches. Her exam shows no focal deficits. She still has some mild to moderate headaches and mild lightheadedness. What is the next best step?",
    "option_a": "MRI brain with and without contrast",
    "option_b": "CT head without contrast",
    "option_c": "CT head with and without contrast",
