    "question_text": "20 year old man with no significant past medical history presents with episodic headaches for the past 4 years. He has no family history of headaches. He describes his headaches as very intense, occurring daily in the last 6 months, with a typical duration of at least 5 hours. Headaches are unilateral and are associated with nausea. He has no tearing or runny nose. His exam is unremarkable for focal deficits. What is the acute treatment of choice?",
