    "question_text": "A 24 year old woman presents with numbness of the left arm. On exam, she has no cranial nerve or motor deficits. Her only abnormal finding is decreased sensation in the left arm along the lateral arm to the thumb. She notes that when she bends her head forward there is a sharp shooting pain down her spine. She has not had symptoms like this in the past. What is the next best step?",
