    "question_text": "A 25 year old woman presents for evaluation of right facial pain. When she chews or brushes she gets sharp shooting electricity-like pain in the right face. Wind blowing on her face can trigger the pain easily. She has an abnormal MRI brain showing 2 oval shaped T2 hyperintense lesions in the periventricular region and 1 in the brainstem. One of the periventricular lesions is enhancing. What would be the best next step?",
