    "explanation": "The correct answer is E. Aseptic Meningitis. The common side effects of Interferon-­beta medications are injection site reaction and flu-like symptoms. Depression, liver toxicity, and leukopenia are also adverse effects to warn the patient of and monitor. Baseline and periodic monitoring of their cell counts and liver functions are important. Aseptic meningitis is not a common side effect of the medication (Ontaneda and Fox 2013). References Berkovic RR, Krieger SC. Multiple sclerosis and other demyelinating diseases. Acute multiple sclerosis relapse. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2016;22(3):799–814. Feroze KB, Wang J. Internuclear ophthalmoplegia. Treasure Island: StatPearls; 2018. Fix JD. Chapter 17, visual system. In: (3rd ed.) High-yield neuroanatomy high-yield series. 3rd ed. Riverwoods: Lippincott Williams and Wilkins; 2014. p. 125. Frohman TC, et al. Neurotherapeutic strategies for multiple sclerosis. Neurol Clin. 2016;34(3):483–523. Katz Sand I. Neuromyelitis optica spectrum disorders. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2016;22(3, Multiple Sclerosis and Other Demyelinating Diseases):864–96. Khare S, Seth D. Lhermitte’s sign: the current status. Ann Indian Acad Neurol. 2015;18(2): 154–6. Krieger SC. New approaches to the diagnosis, clinical course, and goals of therapy in multiple sclerosis and related disorders. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2016;22(3.), Multiple sclerosis and other demyelinating diseases):723–9. Neuteboom R, et al. The spectrum of inflammatory acquired demyelinating syndromes in children. Semin Pediatr Neurol. 2017;24(3):189–200. Okuda DT, Krieger SC. Multiple sclerosis and other demyelinating diseases. Incidental lesions suggesting multiple sclerosis. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2016;22(3):730–43. Ontaneda D, Fox RJ. Multiple sclerosis treatment: risk mitigation. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2013;19(4):1092–9.",
