    "question_text": "A patient comes in after having a seizure. She has left mesial temporal sclerosis. She was well controlled on lamotrigine. Her last seizure was 1 year ago. She is on no other medications. What is not a common reason for this breakthrough seizure?",
    "option_a": "Missed dose of medication",
