    "question_text": "A 67 year old woman presents with her family for memory loss. Daughter says patient seems more forgetful and repetitive during conversations. She has forgotten to pay a few bills, which is very unusual for her and has been getting lost while driving a few times. She quit work 2 years ago because she was making mistakes. Her Montreal Cognitive Assessment shows a score of 24/30 for recall of 4 items but was able to recall with cueing, 1 for drawing a cube, and the date. Her MRI brain shows mild hippocampal atrophy. Which allele of the APOE gene predisposes this patient to a higher risk of Alzheimer’s Dementia?",
