    "correct_option": "D",
    "explanation": "The correct answer is D. Frontotemporal dementia patients have disinhibition, lack motivation, may make inappropriate comments, lose empathy for others, and may neglect their hygiene. Other characteristics include a craving for sweets and overeating. In the non-fluent variant, patients have prominent signs of language dysfunction. Patients will present with symptoms similar to a patient with expressive aphasia with grammatical errors and impaired comprehension (Bang et al. 2015).",
