    "explanation": "The correct answer is B. This patient most likely has Guillain-Barré syndrome. IVIG and Plasma exchange have been shown in randomized controlled trials to be equally effective for the treatment of GBS and improving outcomes. It is recommended to admit Guillain-Barré syndrome patients to at least telemetry monitoring to monitor for dysautonomia (“Randomised trial of plasma exchange, intravenous immunoglobulin, and combined treatments in Guillain-­ Barre syndrome. Plasma Exchange/Sandoglobulin Guillain-Barre Syndrome Trial Group,” 1997; Yuki and Hartung 2012).",
