    "question_text": "A 4 year-old boy presents with toe-walking to a pediatric neurology clinic. On your examination, you have him sit on the floor and note that he uses his hands to climb up his body to get to a standing position. You also notice large calves. Creatine kinase levels from his local pediatrician were 10,000. Normal values at your laboratory are less than 143. He has a normal sensory exam and normal reflexes. Which of the following options would NOT be a well-studied intervention considered at some point in this boy’s future?",
