    "question_text": "A 31 year-old woman presents to the ER with weakness of her bilateral lower extremities, difficulty with urination and constipation for 3 days, which is unusual for her. A post-void residual Foley catheterization reveals 1 liter of urine. On examination, she has a sensory level to her umbilicus, weakness in her bilateral lower extremities (proximally and distally), and clonus at her bilateral ankles. Her rectal tone is reduced. Examination of her upper extremities includes normal strength, sensation and reflexes. Which of the following is the next best step for this patient?",
