    "question_text": "A 57 year old right-handed man is found collapsed behind the wheel of his vehicle by bystanders. Upon ED evaluation he is drowsy, able to follow commands, with left homonymous hemianopsia, right mild facial paresis, right upper extremity and right lower extremity pronator drift, moderate spatial hemineglect. INR is 1.2, platelets 230. EKG shows sinus bradycardia. CT head demonstrates a hyperdensity in the M1 right middle cerebral artery and moderate cerebral edema in lateral temporal lobe. What is the next immediate step in management?",
