    "question_text": "A 60 year-old woman with uncontrolled hypertension, active smoker, alcohol abuse, presents to the emergency room with severe headache, nausea and droopy left eyelid. On exam she has evidence of left eyelid ptosis, left pupil 5 mm and sluggishly reactive, right pupil 3 mm brisk, extraocular movements abnormal with preserved left eye abduction, at rest appearing “down and out”. She suddenly becomes obtunded, and with respiratory depression, left pupil fixed and dilated. Stat CT head shows diffuse subarachnoid hemorrhage. She is emergently taken to the angiography suite to evaluate for treatment of which suspected source of aneurysmal rupture?",
