    "question_text": "A 35 year-old man presents with new onset generalized convulsive seizure. After recovering he states that he has had new headache for the past 3 months. Examination shows he is alert, has a flat affect and positive jaw jerk. Imaging shows a dural-based homogeneously enhancing mass. What treatment options would be necessary to improve outcome?",
