    "explanation": "The correct answer is D. Traumatic brain injury is a common cause of death and chronic disability. Causes of TBI include falls, MVA, contact sports and non-­ accidental trauma. Falls are common in the very young and in older adults. Non-­ accidental trauma should be sought as a cause in younger age patients. Sports injuries and motor vehicle accident as cause of traumatic injury are more common in adolescents (Ling et al. 2010).",
