    "explanation": "The correct answer is F. Reactive pupils and lack of apnea are the elements of the examination not compatible with brain death. For determination of brain death, an irreversible cause to neurologic injury proximate to coma is established; here a major ischemic stroke causing cerebral edema and midline shift. Examination is done when the patient is normothermic and normotensive. In the clinical evaluation there is no evidence of responsiveness to external stimuli. Brainstem reflexes are tested, with absence of pupil constriction, corneal reflex, lack of gag and any oculocephalic maneuver to meet criteria. Additionally, for formal brain death evaluation the oculovestibular reflex can be tested with cold caloric testing, implemented with water irrigation into the ear canal. Apnea is the absence of the respiratory drive that is a component of brain death assessment (Wijdicks et al. 2010).",
