    "question_text": "A 33 year-old man with AIDS (CD4 count 160) presents because of malaise, low-grade fever and headache for several months. He has no prior headache history. He states he has been having night sweats, chills and weight loss for 4 months. He has a fever of 100 F, photophobia and mild neck stiffness, and no other focal signs on examination. Labs show no leukocytosis or thrombocytosis. CT head shows no focal lesions. CSF shows an opening pressure of 30, wbc 132, protein 113, and glucose 33. What other testing would NOT be relevant in this clinical case?",
