    "question_text": "A 40 year-old man comes home from work because of feeling malaise, in the morning. At lunch his wife comes home and finds him in bed, sweating and ill-­ appearing. Upon arrival to the ED his temperature is 102 F, he is awake but lethargic, and has a non-blanching purpuric rash throughout his body. Both Kernig’s and Brudzinki signs are positive. CT brain is negative for acute findings. A lumbar puncture is done with opening pressure 30, turbid CSF, wbc 432, rbc 3, protein 100 (elevated) and glucose 24 (low). What step(s) is/are needed in management?",
