    "explanation": "The correct answer is A. Toxoplasmosis. Toxoplasmosis occurs commonly in HIV patients with CD4 counts less than 200 cells/mm3. CNS toxoplasmosis has a predilection for the basal ganglia and can be a ring-enhancing lesion with mass effect. Lymphoma is in the differential but is not an infectious cause. Coccidiodes and aspergillosis are fungal infections that can cause CNS infection but have alternative radiographic features (Saylor 2018). 14 Meningitis and Encephalitis References Athar P, Hasbun R, Nolan MS, Salazar L, Woods SP, Sheikh K, Murray KO. Long-term neuromuscular outcomes of west nile virus infection: a clinical and electromyographic evaluation of patients with a history of infection. [Case Reports]. Muscle Nerve. 2018;57(1):77–82. https:// doi.org/10.1002/mus.25660. Beckham J, Solbrig M, Tyler K. Chapter 53B. Infections of the nervous system: viral encephalitis and meningitis. In: Bradley’s neurology in clinical practice. 5th ed. Philadelphia: Elsevier Inc; 2008. p. 1231–58. Bell M, Khandji A, Iwamoto F. Chapter 17. Focal mass lesions. In: Merritt’s neurology. 13th ed. Philadelphia: Wolters Kluwer; 2016. p. 303. Cho T. Helminthic infections of the central nervous system. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2018;24(5, Neuroinfectious disease):1489–511. Chow F. Brain and spinal epidural abscess. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2018;24(5, Neuroinfectious disease):1327–48. Harati Y, Bosch P. Chapter 80. Disorders of peripheral nerves. In: Bradley’s neurology in clinical practice. 5th ed. Philadelphia: Elsevier Inc; 2008. p. 2343. Koshy A, Roos K. Chapter 53C. Infections of the nervous system: bacterial and fungal. In: Bradley’s neurology in clinical practice. 5th ed. Philadelphia: Elsevier Inc; 2008. p. 1259–67. Mara C. Infections of the central nervous system in patients with HIV. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2006;12(2):111–32. Panackal A, Williamson P. Fungal Infections of the central nervous system. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2015;21(6 Neuroinfectious disease):1662–78. Popovic N, Milosevic B, Urosevic A, Poluga J, Stevanovic G, Milosevic I, Lavadinovic L, Nikolic J, Dulovic O. Clinical characteristics and functional outcome of patients with West Nile neuroinvasive disease in Serbia. J Neurol. 2014;261(6):1104–11. https://doi.org/10.1007/ s00415-014-7318-7. Roos K, Greenlee J. Meningitis and encephalitis. Continuum Lifelong Learn Neurol. 2011;17(5):1010–23. Saylor D. Neurologic complications of human immunodeficiency virus. Continuum (Minneap Minn). 2018;24(5, Neuroinfectious disease):1397–421. Solbrig M, Tyler K. Chapter 57B. Infections of the nervous system. Viral infections. In: Neurology in clinical practice. 5th ed. Philadelphia: Elsevier Inc; 2008. p. 1472–4.",
