    "question_text": "A 40 year-old woman with metastatic multiple myeloma presents because of confusion, abdominal pain and personality changes reported by her family. She has generalized weakness and recent hospitalization for kidney stones. On examination she is lethargic, and the only finding on exam is proximal muscle weakness. MRI brain is normal. Notable labs causative for encephalopathy and presentation are:",
