    "question_text": "A 32 year-old woman, who has long-standing alcoholism, chronic pain and anxiety was found by her roommate unresponsive. Several empty pill bottles were found next to her at the scene when paramedics arrive. GCS is 6, blood glucose is 113, blood pressure 102/68, and respirations are shallow. What potential agents can be administered to attempt to improve her condition?",
